  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing inclusive education systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &#x201c;Developing Inclusive Education Systems: What We Know and What We Do to Enhance Learning of Students with Disabilities&#x201d; supports RIINEE member countries in strengthening inclusive education policies and practices to improve the learning opportunities and well-being of students with disabilities. Aligned with SDG 4 and international human rights frameworks, the project focuses on three key areas: improving monitoring through the implementation of the updated SIRIED framework, strengthening the capacities of education professionals and teachers through training and peer-learning initiatives, and fostering regional cooperation through RIINEE. By promoting evidence-based policies, inclusive pedagogies, innovative practices and regional dialogue, the project contributes to advancing the right to quality education and ensuring that every learner matters and matters equally.</narrative>
  </description>
